K=0 (background pi only): cyclic count = 6, set = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
K=1 (reroute 1->5):        cyclic count = 3, set = [4, 5, 6]
K=2 (also reroute 3->2):   cyclic count = 5, set = [2, 3, 4, 5, 6]

K=1 -> K=2 (adding ONE more reroute): cyclic count went 3 -> 5 (INCREASE)
COUNTEREXAMPLE CONFIRMED: adding a reroute can strictly INCREASE the cyclic count.
Hence {cyclic count} is not pathwise monotone in K (equivalently, in c under the
natural Poissonization coupling) -- see ATTEMPT.md Section 4.2.
